ow we have a forest of trees, Let "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cum"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"] be the xor of the weights on the edges in the path from the root of the component of node "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" to node "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". Calculate it using dfs. To find the relation between 2 words "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"u"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"v"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", Check if they are in the same component using union-find, If they aren't, The answer is 3 otherwise the answer is "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/1aef6a0dee14b59b16ccae269412c8acb40c39ed18c40e18bc283c59218ea87a.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":", Now to answer suspended relations, Find the relation between the 2 words and check if it's the same as the input relation, Then answer the queries."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Code : "},{"attrs":{"href":"http://pastebin.com/WqwduaYs"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"http://pastebin.com/WqwduaYs"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Time complexity : "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"(("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" + "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"m"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" + "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"q"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":")"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"log"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") * "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"maxL"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") where "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"maxL"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" is the length of the longest string considering that union-find works in constant time."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Problem author : "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/profile/mahmoudbadawy"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"mahmoudbadawy"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Solution author : me."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Testers : me and "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/profile/mahmoudbadawy"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"mahmoudbadawy"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Wait for a hard version of this problem."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/766/problem/E"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"766E - Mahmoud and a xor trip"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If we have an array "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"ans"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"] which represents the number of paths that makes the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"th"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"superscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" bit sit to 1, Our answer will be "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/cd5c20f097493c8c98591440e8b7aee76db520f2e5aca49ea3b0426eea433730.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"arr"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"]["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"